# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS — read this block twice.
#
# .env holds your REAL Neon connection string and your JWT signing
# secret. If that file reaches GitHub, your database is publicly
# reachable and every token you ever mint can be forged. It must never
# be committed.
#
# The rules:
#   .env         -> ignored
#   .env.*       -> ignored (every variant: .env.local, .env.production...)
#   !.env.example-> ALLOWED, and you WANT it. It is the template that
#                   tells the next person which variables to set.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore only affects UNTRACKED files. If a secret was already
# committed, adding it here does NOT remove it from history — you would
# need `git rm --cached` plus a history rewrite. So never commit it in
# the first place.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dependencies
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Bun's local cache / install errors
.bun/
bun-error.log*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prisma
#
# src/generated/ is CODE GENERATED by `bun run db:generate`. It is
# rebuilt from prisma/schema.prisma on every install and in CI.
# Committing it means merge conflicts inside a 0.8 MB file that nobody
# wrote by hand, and it can drift from the schema.
#
# NOTE: prisma/migrations/ IS committed — the migration history is the
# source of truth for the database structure.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
src/generated/

# Local SQLite databases (only if you ever point Prisma at a file)
*.db
*.db-journal
prisma/*.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build output
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
out/
*.local

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test + coverage output
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
*.lcov
.nyc_output/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs + runtime junk
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json
*.pid
*.pid.lock
pids/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Caches + scratch files
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
.eslintcache
.temp/
.tmp/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*~

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Certificates + private keys
#
# Not used yet — but the payments phase will need Razorpay/Stripe
# credentials and a webhook secret. Those go in .env, never in the repo.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets.json
*.secret

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors
#
# .vscode/settings.json is allowed through on purpose: it holds the
# files.exclude that hides src/generated/ for everyone on the project.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS files
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini

# direnv
.envrc
